    "narrative": "Our strongest play today is clearly **Bryce Harper**, whose score of 80.21 is buoyed by a favorable matchup against Bieber (5.23 xERA) and an optimal #3 spot in the order. He is our cornerstone for run production today. **Luis Arraez** and **Justin Crawford** also benefit significantly from this same matchup; while **Justin Crawford**\u2019s projection takes a hit due to his #9 slot, his profile remains an elite source of stolen bases, which is critical for our 5x5 objectives. **Masyn Winn** is another high-floor start today (63.90), as he squares off against Lorenzen with a favorable wind blowing out and a pitcher whose delivery speed provides a distinct advantage for our aggressive base-stealing strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Kyle Karros**, who came within a hair of cracking the starting nine. His score of 52.03 was competitive, but he ultimately lost out to the superior platoon efficiency of **Gavin Sheets** and **Dylan Beavers**, who both leverage significant handedness advantages against their respective opponents. While we have concerns about **Yainer Diaz** and **Daulton Varsho** due to their lineups remaining pending, their base projections were sufficient to keep them in the mix. Conversely, **Gleyber Torres** remains a risk; his efficiency has dipped below the 50-point threshold due to a difficult matchup against Webb and an unfavorable platoon split, making him the most likely candidate to be swapped should official lineups reveal a poor batting order placement.",
